## Decisions

### Which of these `/api/do/` fixes should I make?

**What this is.** The TODO item "Audit /api/do endpoints" (issue #180) asks for a review of the `/api/do/` calls: naming, request/response shapes, who may call each, whether each should be a call at all, OpenAPI coverage and tests. `/api/do/` holds the imperative calls that do more than `POST /api/q`'s plain batches of row writes. Every `/api/` route is mounted on every host (`docs/api.md`), and each call works out who may use it for itself. Every call goes through `caller()` (`internal/db/http.go`), which lets in anyone in the directory (by session or bearer token).

I've finished the review and changed nothing yet. There are **19 calls**. The full inventory is below; the fixes worth making are the choices.

